+
+# railway_project_token (Resource)
+
+An environment-scoped Railway project token. The credential is stored in sensitive Terraform state and cannot be recovered through import.
+
+## Example Usage
+
+```terraform
+resource "railway_project" "example" {
+  name = "example"
+}
+
+resource "railway_project_token" "ci" {
+  name           = "GitHub Actions"
+  project_id     = railway_project.example.id
+  environment_id = railway_project.example.default_environment.id
+}
+```
+
+<!-- schema generated by tfplugindocs -->
+## Schema
+
+### Required
+
+- `environment_id` (String) Environment that the token can access. Changing it replaces the token.
+- `name` (String) Human-readable token name. Changing it replaces the token.
+- `project_id` (String) Project that owns the token. Changing it replaces the token.
+
+### Read-Only
+
+- `id` (String) Stable local identifier. The remote token identifier is kept separately so it cannot expose a credential in Terraform's resource summaries.
+- `token` (String, Sensitive) Issued credential. Sensitive values are redacted from normal output but remain in Terraform state and plan artifacts.
+- `token_id` (String, Sensitive) Railway token record identifier. Kept sensitive because the API's credential and record identifiers must not be assumed to differ.
